WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:05.837
To follow a story in a new language, you
need to know about ninety-eight of every
hundred words.

2
00:00:06.237 --> 00:00:08.741
For a beginner, the original is out of
reach.

3
00:00:08.761 --> 00:00:11.547
Graded readers rewrite the story at your
level.

4
00:00:11.997 --> 00:00:15.461
Sotto is a free graded reader that runs in
your browser.

5
00:00:15.611 --> 00:00:18.911
Pick a language, then the hardest sentence
you can still follow.

6
00:00:19.211 --> 00:00:22.535
It hands you a book at that level, like
Cinderella, in French.

7
00:00:22.885 --> 00:00:23.759
Don't know a word?

8
00:00:23.779 --> 00:00:26.611
Tap it for the meaning, and the sentence it
came from.

9
00:00:26.711 --> 00:00:29.105
Save it, and it stays marked on the page.

10
00:00:29.405 --> 00:00:31.678
Press play to hear the chapter read aloud.

11
00:00:31.728 --> 00:00:34.928
[French narration] Une jeune fille habite
avec son père et sa belle-mère.

12
00:00:35.078 --> 00:00:36.932
Each word fills in as it's spoken.

13
00:00:37.332 --> 00:00:37.990
Then, speak.

14
00:00:38.010 --> 00:00:42.455
Talk about the passage out loud, with a
voice tutor that read the same page.

15
00:00:42.655 --> 00:00:47.119
It can quiz you on the story, explain the
grammar, or coach your pronunciation.

16
00:00:47.519 --> 00:00:51.284
Reading, listening, and translations are
free, with no account.

17
00:00:51.304 --> 00:00:53.556
The tutor starts with a free trial.

18
00:00:53.906 --> 00:00:58.436
Read a page, then talk about it. Try Sotto
free, at readsotto.app.
